The booking, the payments and the alerts are a real product, and they're the part I'd be least sure of in a real school. Parents would book through it because they trust the school's name on it. So the school's own rules should decide who can tutor there, and the platform should just follow them. The school's rules may well be stricter than mine, and that's one of the things I'm least sure of, since I don't know which country's laws govern it.

The payment system varies most by country. In some places a card on file for a booking is normal. In others parents pay the tutor directly, and the platform only charges the tutor. Both work, and your local rules decide which. The alert I'd build in the open. A parent who gets a reminder the night before a session is glad of it. Nobody is hidden in it.
